{
  "precondition": "Customer account ID 1 is uniquely confirmed as Joe's Auto Repair with price tier silver. Warehouses are available; no routing requirement was provided, so warehouse ID 1 is a valid selection.",
  "decision_rule": "Create the open sales-order header next using customer_account_id 1, warehouse_id 1, requested_ship_date 2026-01-05, the applicable order date, and a unique order number. Then look up each SKU and call apply_pricing_rules_to_line for each part, quantity, category, customer, and order date before creating its line. Use the returned list price, unit price, and discount percentage; set backorder_status to allow. Make exactly one tool call per turn.",
  "expected_transition": "The next successful call returns a new sales_order ID. Subsequent pricing calls should determine the discounts rather than defaulting them to zero, after which three lines are created for quantities 10, 4, and 2.",
  "recovery_check": "If header creation reports a duplicate order number, retrieve that order before retrying to avoid duplicate headers. After all line calls, list the order lines and verify exactly three SKUs with the requested quantities, pricing-rule results, and backorder_status allow."
}
